From: openEuler package contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Export C++ ABI mode definitions through the imported target
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
Source: https://github.com/google/nsync/blob/5b420ef6b16532a4fad4be1fde8e483b6b7bd8f4/CMakeLists.txt
Source-archive-SHA256: bb9b1823f6246afd7e7a78497c43ffca62970c94cfebe39c3d58d3a70850a7bd
Applies-to: nsync 1.30.0 (annotated tag 55155ca0281c59b226d43585babaecc627613db3)
Upstream-status: Not submitted; no upstream write was performed.

The C++ library compiles with NSYNC_ATOMIC_CPP11, so nsync_once is
std::atomic<uint32_t>. The stock public header instead declares uint32_t
when that definition is not inherited. Namespace-scoped once functions
therefore have distinct public C++ parameter types for producer and consumer.
PRIVATE definitions are not exported as target usage requirements.

Use PUBLIC to retain the producer definitions and also export them. This is
a general CMake SDK interface correction, not a RISC-V-only source defect,
observed target failure, CVE, or native ABI success claim. The C target and
all26 original C/C++ CTest invocations are unchanged. Keep the stock consumer;
do not conceal the issue with manually forced consumer definitions.

Original Apache-2.0 source notices and the complete grant are retained before
patching. The adjacent comment records the downstream CMake modification.
Remove when a fixed upstream release exports the same ABI mode requirements
and stock build/installed C/C++ consumers plus the original26 tests pass.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -45 +45,2 @@
-	target_compile_definitions ("${tgtname}" PRIVATE "${NSYNC_CPP_DEFINITIONS}")
+	# Downstream openEuler: export the public C++ ABI mode definitions.
+	target_compile_definitions ("${tgtname}" PUBLIC "${NSYNC_CPP_DEFINITIONS}")
